/**
 * Verifies the password; opens a server-side session — or, story 6-1b, asks for the second factor first
 *
 * Story 6-1a: a session answer also sets the httpOnly refresh cookie (`wms_refresh`, path /api/v1/tenants/session). Attempts are counted per (email, client IP) BEFORE the password check: 5 consecutive failures lock that pair for 15 minutes (423 for any password, real or unknown email alike); 300 attempts a minute per client IP answer 429. Story 6-1b: a user with two-factor sign-in set up gets `TotpChallengeResponse`; an owner who has not set it up yet gets `EnrollChallengeResponse` — both create no session and set no cookie, and are completed at `POST /tenants/sign-in/second-factor`. Clients tell the arms apart by the presence of `challenge`. A web client that can complete the second step sends `X-WMS-Second-Factor: 1`; without it, a sign-in that needs the second step answers 409 `client-outdated` and writes nothing.
 */
